{
  "_note": "Example menu, not read by anything - deliberately NOT an active composer.json. universal-frappe-ci composes only when a committed composer.json exists at the repo root, so seeding an active file would trigger a compose the moment the shell lands. Activate deliberately: copy this file to composer.json, keep only the modules you need, and rename the app to a valid Frappe app name (Python identifier - underscores, no hyphens). Frappe compose is normally driven by the registry templates in The-Rokct-Protocol (core/utils/frappe/composer/*.json); the modules below are copied verbatim (refs, pins and per-entry commentary included) from that registry's rokctapp.json, so some _comment text is rokctapp-specific.",
  "name": "{{APP_SLUG}}",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Known Frappe compose modules for RokctAI products - an example menu for the {{APP_NAME}} app",
  "modules": [
    {
      "name": "base",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/core",
      "path": "../core/base/frappe",
      "ref": "main"
    },
    {
      "name": "auth",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/Users",
      "path": "../Users/auth/frappe",
      "ref": "main"
    },
    {
      "name": "users",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/Users",
      "path": "../Users/users/frappe",
      "ref": "main"
    },
    {
      "name": "subscriptions",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/agent",
      "path": "../agent/subscriptions/frappe",
      "ref": "d549e49345ddac463636da0ccb59395c1c5eb315"
    },
    {
      "name": "gateways",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/pay",
      "path": "../pay/gateways/frappe",
      "ref": "a09501d9f5ddd26d2d2db71ed45c10a6312ccc6f",
      "_comment": "Same pay pin as erp/hrms/wallet below: the composer clones one ref per repo, so every pay module entry must share it. Replaces the retired 'pay' entry (../pay/payments/frappe no longer carries a frappe module or manifest.json): pay's payments/frappe content moved into the gateways and wallet modules, so this template mirrors rcore.json's wallet+gateways pair."
    },
    {
      "name": "telemetry",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/core",
      "path": "../core/telemetry/frappe",
      "ref": "main"
    },
    {
      "name": "comms",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/core",
      "path": "../core/comms/frappe",
      "ref": "main"
    },
    {
      "name": "wallet",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/pay",
      "path": "../pay/wallet/frappe",
      "ref": "a09501d9f5ddd26d2d2db71ed45c10a6312ccc6f"
    },
    {
      "name": "erp",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/pay",
      "path": "../pay/erp/frappe",
      "ref": "a09501d9f5ddd26d2d2db71ed45c10a6312ccc6f",
      "_comment": "ERPNext v16 fork flattened into one composed module (fork of frappe/erpnext via Frappenize/erpnext@rokct-hotfix). Upstream crm/projects/support modules are excluded and resolve to the productivity repo's SDK modules; the five fleet-colliding doctypes (Branch, Brand, Delivery Settings, Subscription, Subscription Settings + dependents) are excluded per pay#35's collision review, so erp composes beside base/subscriptions/products/delivery. A site composed with this module must NOT also have upstream erpnext installed. Pinned at the pay head carrying the fleet-collision exclusion; strict-compose verified at this SHA."
    },
    {
      "name": "hrms",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/pay",
      "path": "../pay/hrms/frappe",
      "ref": "a09501d9f5ddd26d2d2db71ed45c10a6312ccc6f",
      "_comment": "Frappe HR fork (via Frappenize/hrms@rokct-hotfix). Composes ONLY alongside the erp module above — the Employee master and accounting doctypes live in erp, and every upstream erpnext reference resolves to {app_name}.erp. Never add hrms to a template without erp. Same pay pin as erp."
    },
    {
      "name": "crm",
      "enabled": true,
      "source": "git",
      "git": "https://github.com/RokctAI/productivity",
      "path": "../productivity/crm/frappe",
      "ref": "main",
      "_comment": "Core CRM slice (leads, deals, contacts, organizations, notes, tasks, call logs, statuses) ported from Frappenize/crm (frappe/crm fork) into the productivity SDK. Composing this module replaces installing the standalone frappe/crm app — a site must NOT have frappe/crm installed alongside rcore, since the doctype names (CRM Lead, CRM Deal, ...) are intentionally identical and would double-define. Existing sites need one 'bench execute rcore.patches.crm_seed_defaults.execute' to seed default statuses."
    }
  ]
}
